      "text": "This is a geometric series with first term $a = 1$ and common ratio $r = 2$. The sum of a geometric series can be found using the formula $S = \\frac{a(1 - r^n)}{1 - r}$. Plugging in $a$, $r$, and $n = 10$ (since there are 10 terms in the series), we get \\begin{align*}\nS &= \\frac{1(1 - 2^{10})}{1 - 2} \\\\\n  &= \\frac{1(1 - 1024)}{1 - 2} \\\\\n  &= \\frac{-1023}{-1} \\\\\n  &= \\boxed{1023}\n\\end{align*}. The answer is 1023",
